T:Every Breath You Take
C:Sting (The Police)
M:4/4
O:England, 1983
N:Verse (bars 1-8) and bridge (bars 9-16). Melody from channel 3 of a MIDI arrangement (hamienet.com, track 5129; the vocal line, E4 to B5); chords from its guitar and bass channels. Transposed down a major third from A to F, so the lowest note (E4) lands on C4 and the highest (B5) on G5. Humanized onsets snapped to the sixteenth grid. Releases a sixteenth short of the next note are filled in; the held notes (2.5 and 3.25 beats in the source) are written as 2 and 3 beats. The Eb5 in bar 15 is the source's G5, which is outside the key of A. Bar 11 is B-flat 7 because the arrangement's bass plays a natural C there (D7 in A).
